      "id": 18097,
      "patch": {
        "description": "Yellow Pine Solar III’s 2026 Nevada application describes 100 MWac of solar and 225 MW of storage on 1,008.94 acres. It targets Q2 2026 construction and Q2 2027 operation. Nevada approved tax abatements June 3; a June 4 eligibility certificate and June 4–5 signatures confirm the agreement. Conflicting investment scopes and the actual construction stage remain unresolved.",
        "longFormSummary": "<h3>Phase-specific filing</h3><ul><li>Yellow Pine Solar III LLC’s 2026 Nevada application describes a 100 MWac solar facility co-located with 225 MW of battery storage in Clark County. The site is 1,008.94 acres at 6901 Tecopa Road. Solar generation and storage power are separate ratings; no storage duration is inferred.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/yps3-reta-redacted.pdf\"></cite></li></ul><h3>Schedule and regulatory process</h3><ul><li>The application anticipates construction beginning in Q2 2026 and commercial operation in Q2 2027. The June 3 tax-abatement hearing does not verify that physical construction has started or that the facility is operational.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/yps3-reta-redacted.pdf\"></cite></li><li>Nevada’s June 3 hearing minutes identify this application as AFN 26-0401SPV and record approval of the partial tax-abatement application. No public comments were made at either public-comment period.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/hearing-minutes-yellow-pine-solar-iii-llc.pdf\"></cite></li></ul><h3>Cost conflict</h3><ul><li>The application lists USD 583.6 million total capital investment, with 25% expended in Nevada. The hearing minutes instead record approximately USD 149.9 million investment in the facility. These are not treated as interchangeable construction budgets; price remains unpublished pending reconciliation of the scope and final agreement.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/yps3-reta-redacted.pdf\"></cite></li><li>The state index’s link labelled Legal Order opens a Libra Solar order rather than a Yellow Pine III order. The wrong-project document is excluded from this profile.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/programs/renewable-energy-tax-abatement-reta-program/renewable-energy-tax-abatement-projects-2026/\"></cite></li></ul><h3>Executed tax-abatement records</h3><ul><li>The executed agreement identifies Yellow Pine Solar III and application AFN 26-0401SPV, made June 3, 2026. Its signature page shows the state director signing June 4 and the owner signing June 5. It authorizes partial tax abatements; it does not establish physical construction, commissioning or a reconciled construction budget.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/final-abatement-agreement_yellow-pine-solar-iii-llc---executed.pdf\"></cite></li><li>The eligibility certificate is signed and effective June 4, 2026. This is the correct project’s tax-eligibility record, separate from the state index’s wrong-project Legal Order hyperlink.<cite data-ref=\"https://www.energy.nv.gov/contentassets/ecb91b2330d345a1bc872bc879534cbd/final-coe_yellow-pine-solar-iii-llc---jh-signed.pdf\"></cite></li></ul>"
      },
